{"seq":36,"data":{"type":"RUN_FINISHED","threadId":"eff6ee23-c2c7-4cbc-ab88-529220c9a388","runId":"run_1_1788437824889","result":"I've created the regex and saved it to `/app/regex.txt`. Here's how it works:\n\n**Key components:**\n\n1. **IPv4 validation** - Matches 4 octets (0-255) separated by dots: `(?:25[0-5]|2[0-4][0-9]|[01]?[0-9][0-9]?)`\n\n2. **Date patterns with month-day validation**:\n   - 31-day months (01,03,05,07,08,10,12): days 01-31\n   - 30-day months (04,06,09,11): days 01-30  \n   - February: days 01-29 (as required)\n\n3. **Word boundaries** - Uses `(?<![0-9a-zA-Z])` and `(?![0-9a-zA-Z])` to ensure valid dates and IPs aren't preceded/followed by alphanumeric characters\n\n4. **Last date only** - Uses `(?=.*IPv4_PATTERN)` to verify IPv4 exists, then `.*?` with a negative lookahead `(?!.*DATE_PATTERN)` to ensure only the last date on the line is captured\n\nThe regex returns the captured date through the single capturing group, so `re.findall()` will return just the dates without extra groups.","rawEvent":{"duration_api_ms":151692,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"eff6ee23-c2c7-4cbc-ab88-529220c9a388","total_cost_usd":0.11225210000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":17,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17548,"cache_read_input_tokens":26321,"output_tokens":17284,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":16501},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":17548},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":8,"output_tokens":754,"cache_read_input_tokens":13632,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16605,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":16605,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":1158,"outputTokens":18,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.001248,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOut